ms":["crazy about","furious with"],"antonyms":["indifferent to","calm"]}},{"lemma":"married to","kind":"adjectives","source":"tools/en/verb-prep/data/adjectives.json","data":{"word_type":"adjective","prepositions":["to"],"pattern":"be + married to + [someone]","level":"A1","definition":"Joined in marriage to a specific person.","grammar_rule":"Always use 'to' after 'married'. Using 'with' is a very common translation error from other languages.","examples":["She has been married to Mark for ten years.","Who is David married to?"],"common_mistake":"❌ She is married with a doctor. ➜ ✅ She is married to a doctor.","synonyms":["wedded to","betrothed to"],"antonyms":["single","divorced from","unmarried"],"related_forms":"⚡ Adjective: 'married to John' ➔ Related Verb: 'marry'"}},{"lemma":"map of","kind":"nouns","source":"tools/en/verb-prep/data/nouns.json","data":{"word_type":"noun","prepositions":["of"],"pattern":"map of + [city / country / area]","level":"A1","definition":"A diagrammatic representation of an area of land or sea.","grammar_rule":"Always use 'of' after 'map' when identifying the geographical area.","examples":["Do you have a street map of central London?","The tour guide handed us a map of the national park."],"common_mistake":"❌ Here is a map for the subway. ➜ ✅ Here is a map of the subway.","synonyms":["chart of","plan of"],"antonyms":["uncharted territory","unmapped area"]}},{"lemma":"member of","kind":"nouns","source":"tools/en/verb-prep/data/nouns.json","data":{"word_type":"noun","prepositions":["of"],"pattern":"member of + [group / club / family / team]","level":"A1","definition":"An individual belonging to a group, organization, or society.","grammar_rule":"Always use 'of' after 'member' when indicating the organization or group.","examples":["She has been an active member of the sports club for two years.","Every member of the team worked hard."],"common_mistake":"❌ He is a member in our club. ➜ ✅ He is a member of our club.","synonyms":["part of","participant in"],"antonyms":["non-member of","outsider to"]}},{"lemma":"monopoly on","kind":"nouns","source":"tools/en/verb-prep/data/nouns.json","data":{"word_type":"noun","prepositions":["on","of"],"pattern":"monopoly on/of + [market / trade / truth]","level":"B2","definition":"The exclusive possession or control of the supply of or trade in a commodity or service.","grammar_rule":"Use 'monopoly ON' or 'monopoly OF'.","examples":["No single company should have a monopoly on energy supplies.","Scientists do not claim a monopoly on truth."],"common_mistake":"❌ A monopoly for electricity. ➜ ✅ A monopoly on electricity.","synonyms":["domination of","exclusive control of"],"antonyms":["competition in"]}},{"lemma":"make","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"make","past_simple":"made","past_participle":"made","third_person_singular":"makes","pattern_group":"same_past_participle","level":"A1","definition":"To create, construct, or produce.","examples":["She makes delicious cakes.","He made a wooden chair in workshop.","They have made great progress."],"subgroup":"base_past_past","vowel_pattern":"a-a-a"}},{"lemma":"marry","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/verb-prep/data/verbs.json","data":{"is_phrasal":false,"transitivity":"Transitive","transitivity_code":"VT","prepositions":["none"],"pattern":"marry [someone] (direct object)","level":"A1","definition":"To join in marriage with someone.","grammar_rule":"Direct transitive verb in active voice! Do NOT add 'with' or 'to' after active 'marry'.","noun_parallel":"⚡ Active Verb: 'He married her' (no prep) ➔ Passive Adjective: 'He is married TO her'","examples":["Will you marry me?","She married her high school sweetheart last year."],"common_mistake":"❌ He married with a lawyer. ➔ ✅ He married a lawyer.","synonyms":["wed","espouse"],"antonyms":["divorce"],"preposition_structure":"none","particle_count":0}},{"lemma":"mean","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"mean","past_simple":"meant","past_participle":"meant","third_person_singular":"means","pattern_group":"same_past_participle","level":"A1","definition":"To signify or intend to express.","examples":["What does this word mean in context?","He meant to call you earlier today.","She has meant well all along."],"subgroup":"base_past_past","vowel_pattern":"e-e-e"}},{"lemma":"meet","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"meet","past_simple":"met","past_participle":"met","third_person_singular":"meets","pattern_group":"vowel_change","level":"A1","definition":"To encounter or assemble with someone.","examples":["She meets her friends every weekend.","He met the director yesterday morning.","We have met before at a conference."],"subgroup":"base_past_past","vowel_pattern":"e-e-e"}},{"lemma":"mislay","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"mislay","past_simple":"mislaid","past_participle":"mislaid","third_person_singular":"mislays","pattern_group":"same_past_participle","level":"B2","definition":"To lose temporarily or misplace.","examples":["He mislays his glasses frequently.","She mislaid important document folder.","I have mislaid my house keys."],"subgroup":"base_past_past","vowel_pattern":"i-i-i"}},{"lemma":"mislead","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"mislead","past_simple":"misled","past_participle":"misled","third_person_singular":"misleads","pattern_group":"vowel_change","level":"B2","definition":"To lead astray or deceive.","examples":["False ads mislead consumers easily.","The map misled hikers into woods.","Public has been misled by claims."],"subgroup":"base_past_past","vowel_pattern":"i-i-i"}},{"lemma":"misspell","kind":"verbs","source":"tools/en/irregular-verbs/data/verbs.json","data":{"base":"misspell","past_simple":"misspelt","past_participle":"misspelt","third_person_singular":"misspells","pattern_group":"s